egral as\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{3}^{6}\\frac{9}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-3}}\\,\\text{d}x=3\\sqrt{3}{\\int }_{3}^{6}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{(\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{3}})}^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nThis integral resembles the basic integral for inverse hyperbolic cosine,\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{u}^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{arcosh}⁡u+C.\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of ${u}^{2}$ as the variable, we have ${(\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{3}})}^{2}.$\n\nSo, let's substitute $u=\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{3}}.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\sqrt{3}\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nBefore substituting, we use the table below to change the limits from $x$ to $u.$\n\n| $x$ | $3$ | $6$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $\\sqrt{3}$ | $2\\sqrt{3}$ |\n\nUsing the above, we can now write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{3}^{6}\\frac{9}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-3}}\\,\\text{d}x & =3\\sqrt{3}{\\int }_{3}^{6}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{(\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{3}})}^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3\\sqrt{3}{\\int }_{\\sqrt{3}}^{2\\sqrt{3}}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{u}^{2}-1}}\\cdot (\\sqrt{3}\\,\\text{d}u) \\\\  & =9{\\int }_{\\sqrt{3}}^{2\\sqrt{3}}\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\sqrt{{u}^{2}-1}} \\\\  & =9\\operatorname{arcosh}⁡u{|}_{\\sqrt{3}}^{2\\sqrt{3}} \\\\  & =9(\\operatorname{arcosh}⁡2\\sqrt{3}-\\operatorname{arcosh}⁡\\sqrt{3}) \\\\  & =9(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2\\sqrt{3}+\\sqrt{{(2\\sqrt{3})}^{2}-1})-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\sqrt{3}+\\sqrt{{(\\sqrt{3})}^{2}-1})) \\\\  & =9(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2\\sqrt{3}+\\sqrt{11})-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\sqrt{3}+\\sqrt{2})) \\\\  & =9\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{2\\sqrt{3}+\\sqrt{11}}{\\sqrt{3}+\\sqrt{2}})\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535242 true] [17592186339508 1000 #edb/ref 17592186339509 13194139535242 true] [17592186339508 1000 #edb/ref 17592186339510 13194139535242 true] [17592186339508 1000 #edb/ref 17592186339511 13194139535242 true] [17592186339508 1000 #edb/ref 17592186339512 13194139535242 true] [17592186339