 "This integral resembles the basic integral for the inverse hyperbolic sine,\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{u}^{2}+1}}\\,\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡u+C.\n$$\n\n \n\nThe only difference is that instead of ${u}^{2}$ as the variable, we have $36{x}^{2}=(6x)^{2}.$\n\nSo, let's substitute $u=6x.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=6\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{6}\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and compute it, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{36{x}^{2}+1}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{(6x)^{2}+1}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{{u}^{2}+1}}\\,\\cdot (\\frac{1}{6}\\,\\text{d}u) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{u}^{2}+1}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡u+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡6x+C\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535242 true] [17592186339515 1000 #edb/ref 17592186339516 13194139535242 true] [17592186339515 1000 #edb/ref 17592186339517 13194139535242 true] [17592186339515 1000 #edb/ref 17592186339518 13194139535242 true] [17592186339515 1000 #edb/ref 17592186339519 13194139535242 true] [17592186339515 1000 #edb/ref 17592186339520 13194139535242 true] [17592186339515 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535242 true] [17592186339515 1041 "selection" 13194139535242 true] [17592186339515 1104 #edb/ref 17592186339517 13194139535242 true] [17592186339515 1110 #uuid "5fa3d2d1-1e52-57f2-ab28-2cdfbd0662e6" 13194139535242 true] [17592186339516 1034 "3\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡6x+C" 13194139535242 true] [17592186339516 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535242 true] [17592186339516 1111 #uuid "443fa514-7bbb-591a-af19-1e89a638d9c7" 13194139535242 true] [17592186339517 1034 "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡6x+C" 13194139535242 true] [17592186339517 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535242 true] [17592186339517 1111 #uuid "089c9899-5f33-58a3-81f7-4e6fbc35e5be" 1319413953